From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:57:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: test: allocate the host DP tunnels of
 the HBR3 tests with this tree's call

The host DP tunnel helper of the HBR3 tests (from the backport of
39391bb8b5, "thunderbolt: let a lone host DP tunnel run at HBR3, two
share HBR2") passes a data pointer to tb_tunnel_alloc_dp(), as the source
tree does. In this tree tb_tunnel_alloc_dp() takes the callback only (its
callback has the one-argument form, as the backport of d279799da8 notes),
so the USB4 KUnit suite did not build (test.c: too many arguments to
function call, expected 7, have 8). The kernel itself was unaffected: the
recipe configuration does not build the KUnit suite.

Drop the data pointer, as every other tb_tunnel_alloc_dp() call in this
file does.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/test.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/test.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/test.c
index f841813206..178cbaac81 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/test.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/test.c
@@ -4154,7 +4154,7 @@ static struct tb_tunnel *tb_test_cm_dp_tunnel(struct kunit *test, struct tb_test
 	struct tb_tunnel *tunnel;
 	int i;
 
-	tunnel = tb_tunnel_alloc_dp(cm->tb, in, out, 1, 0, 0, tb_test_dp_tunnel_active, NULL);
+	tunnel = tb_tunnel_alloc_dp(cm->tb, in, out, 1, 0, 0, tb_test_dp_tunnel_active);
 	KUNIT_ASSERT_NOT_NULL(test, tunnel);
 	tunnel->host_rate_limit = rate_limit;
 	tunnel->max_rate = min(rate_limit, rate);
